<title>FINLAND: FINNISH 2010 BOND YIELDS 6.70 PCT AT AUCTION.</title>
<headline>FINNISH 2010 BOND YIELDS 6.70 PCT AT AUCTION.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of the</p>
<p>S1/95 bond was announced by the State Treasury Office:</p>
<p> ISSUER:				 Republic of Finland</p>
<p> MATURITY:			     15-10-2010</p>
<p> COUPON:				 8.25 PCT</p>
<p> AUCTION YIELD:			6.70 PCT</p>
<p> PRICE:				  113.40</p>
<p> AUCTION AMOUNT			FIM 60 MLN</p>
<p> BID AMOUNT:			   FIM 260 MLN</p>
<p> PAYMENT FREQUENCY:		  YEARLY</p>
<p>NOTES:</p>
<p>The previous auction of the bond raised 260 million markka</p>
<p>at a price of 115.20 and a yield of 6.53 percent.</p>
<p>After today's auction, the outstanding amount is 3,663</p>
<p>million markka.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
